%% alt: A request's journey in six numbered steps. 1, the browser asks DNS for the site's address. 2, it opens a TCP connection and sets up TLS encryption with the load balancer. 3, it sends the HTTP request. 4, the load balancer forwards it to one of several app servers. 5, the app server checks a cache. 6, only on a miss, it reads the database. The response returns the same way.
%% caption: Every arrow is a network hop. Each one costs time and can fail, and the rest of the guide is about making hops cheaper or safer.
flowchart TB
  classDef control fill:#ede9fe,stroke:#7c3aed,color:#1f1147
  classDef data fill:#fef3c7,stroke:#b45309,color:#3b2405
  classDef cache fill:#fffbeb,stroke:#b45309,stroke-dasharray:6 4,color:#3b2405

  user(["Browser or app"])
  dns["DNS<br/>name → IP address"]
  lb{{"Load balancer"}}:::control
  app["App servers"]
  cache["Cache"]:::cache
  db[("Database")]:::data

  user -- "1 · look up the address" --> dns
  user -- "2 · TCP + TLS handshake<br/>3 · HTTP request" --> lb
  lb -- "4 · forward to one server" --> app
  app -- "5 · check first" --> cache
  app -- "6 · only on a miss" --> db
